{"id": 65, "ts": 1780453945.7531586, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I understand Sarah\u2019s enthusiasm for Candidate\u202fA\u2019s ability to anticipate dangerous situations and see complex connections, but I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fB is the stronger overall fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role.\u202fB\u2019s very conscientious nature and proven ability to handle stress well directly address our top criteria of operational reliability and stress resilience\u2014both essential for international flights. While B is sometimes perceived as pretentious and may adopt the wrong tone, these communication style issues are less critical than the health\u2011related concerns we have for A (unfriendly demeanor and unhealthy eating habits) that could undermine crew cooperation and long\u2011term reliability.\u202fGiven B\u2019s solid technical competence (excellent weather assessment and computer skills) and the lack of any serious safety\u2011relevant deficits, I would continue to recommend Candidate\u202fB."}
