{"id": 77, "ts": 1780454014.6087008, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I appreciate Sarah\u2019s support for Candidate\u202fC and agree that his ability to make correct decisions quickly and stay calm in a crisis is exactly the kind of technical competence and stress resilience we need for long\u2011distance operations. However, his difficulty communicating ideas and the perception that he is egocentric raise serious concerns about crew cooperation and professional communication\u2014both essential for a safe cockpit environment. Compared with Candidate\u202fB, who also handles stress well and is very conscientious, B\u2019s \u201cnasty remarks\u201d about colleagues and weak memory for numbers are also problematic, but they seem more about interpersonal tone and attention rather than the fundamental ability to coordinate decisions under pressure. Given that decision quality and calmness under pressure are weighted heavily for this role, I still lean toward Candidate\u202fC, provided we can address his communication style through training and feedback. I\u2019d welcome any additional observations from Emily on how Candidate\u202fB\u2019s interpersonal issues have manifested in past team settings."}
