{"id": 81, "ts": 1780454036.364553, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fB is our strongest choice. Building on James\u2019s earlier endorsement, I want to highlight that B\u2019s very conscientious nature directly supports operational reliability, and his proven ability to handle stress well addresses the critical stress\u2011resilience criterion for long\u2011distance flights. Moreover, his skill in assessing weather conditions and excellent computer proficiency demonstrate the technical and cognitive competence we need for complex international routes.\nWhile I acknowledge the concern that B can sometimes adopt the wrong tone and is perceived as pretentious, this communication issue is less detrimental than the more serious teamwork and adaptability deficits observed in the other candidates (e.g., C\u2019s difficulty communicating ideas and egocentric attitude, D\u2019s moodiness and loner reputation, A\u2019s unfriendly demeanor). With targeted coaching, B\u2019s tone can be aligned with professional standards, whereas the other candidates present deeper, harder\u2011to\u2011remediate gaps.\nTherefore, I continue to vote for Candidate\u202fB as the best overall fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
